course: dictionary
lesson: 2284
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word crescent can mean more than one thing, so the sentence around it tells you which meaning fits. Look for clues like moon, shape, or street. When you find the clue, try the meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: «In between we see a thin crescent, then a half moon, then a fat gibbous moon.» The words moon and thin are the clues. A crescent here is the thin, curved shape of the Moon when only a little of it is lit.
explain: «Many street names end in Crescent.» Here the clue is street. A crescent is a curved street of houses. Any shape that is curved and thin with pointed ends is also a crescent, such as the cream patch on a bear's chest.
fact: A crescent is a curved shape that is thin and has pointed ends, like a slice of melon.
fact: The crescent Moon is one of the phases of the Moon as it goes around the Earth.
fact: In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, many streets are called Crescent because they curve.
fact: «The Moon makes no light of its own: it is always half lit by the Sun.» We see different amounts of that lit half, from a thin crescent to a full Moon.
fact: Crescent can also be an adjective, as in «a crescent shape».
exercise: «The Moon looked like a thin crescent in the sky.» What is a crescent? | A round ball of light | A straight line of stars | *A curved, thin shape with pointed ends | A dark cloud
exercise: «The Asiatic black bear has a cream-coloured crescent on its chest.» What is the crescent here? | A bear's cave | A ripe nut | A tall tree | *A curved, thin patch of colour
exercise: «We live on Rose Crescent, a street of houses.» What does Crescent mean in this street name? | A small park with a pond | *A curved street of houses | A shop for pets | A busy motorway
test: «The thin new crescent moon was seen at sunset.» Which clue tells you crescent means the Moon's shape? | New, only | Seen | Sunset | *Moon
test: Ella sees a «crescent» on the map next to her house. Which meaning fits best? | A curved street of houses | A sharp hill | *A curved street of houses, in a town where street names end in Crescent | A slice of cake
exam: «Helpers like the Red Cross and Red Crescent stay neutral so they can reach every side.» Which meaning of crescent fits here, and what clue tells you? | *A name used by a helping group, because it is a name for a group that helps people, so the clue is Red Cross and helpers | A shape of a bear's chest, because of the word Red | A thin curved Moon, because of the word moon | A curved street, because of the word Cross
